🛠️ STEP 2: Code Conversion & Fix Rules
When fixing compiler errors across the ported files, strictly enforce the following rules:

Rule A: The Virtual File System (VFile2)
Problem: java.io.File and Minecraft.getMinecraft().mcDataDir will crash or fail to compile in Eaglercraft.
Fix:
Replace all imports of java.io.File with: import net.lax1dude.eaglercraft.v1_8.internal.vfs2.VFile2;
Replace initializations: new File("glide") ➡️ new VFile2("glide").
Replace file creation logic: Remove .mkdir() or .createNewFile(). Replace with: if (!file.exists()) { file.setAllBytes(new byte[0]); }
Rule B: Desktop Dependencies & Libraries
Problem: Missing Apache Commons (ArrayUtils), Netty (ThreadLocalRandom), or desktop sound/logging libraries.
Fix:
Replace io.netty.util.internal.ThreadLocalRandom with java.util.Random.
Remove org.apache.commons.lang3.ArrayUtils. Use standard Java java.util.Arrays or basic loops.
Replace missing logger calls with System.out.println().
Rule C: Rendering & OpenGL
Problem: Standard LWJGL calls (GL11.gl*) cause canvas rendering errors in browser environments.
Fix: Route all render and color operations through Eaglercraft's native state manager: net.minecraft.client.renderer.GlStateManager
